## Report
Validated the suspected introduced UAT false-positive. The checked-out commit is 8ee3f92ccb3fe36c50a54166dd3713cb2aeb4a56. In scripts/uat-s3-tests, wait_for_shard_backfill_completion_metrics still accepts target_pg_id at line 1722, but the success condition at lines 1760-1762 only checks global counters: scan_total, enqueued, written, completed, queue_depth, routine_admitted, and routine_finished. The target PG is only interpolated into the success log. The commit diff confirms the regression: it removed min_pg_backfilled/min_pg_completed parameters and removed per-target-PG latest_metric_family_label_sum checks for event=backfilled and event=complete_succeeded; the PG migration caller now passes only $data_pg without target-PG thresholds. I built a targeted shell PoC that extracts the actual helper and metric parser functions from scripts/uat-s3-tests, stubs metric sampling, and feeds metrics where global backfill counters meet thresholds but only pg-other has per-PG backfilled/complete_succeeded events. Running /workspace/validation_artifacts/argmin-uat-backfill-poc/uat_backfill_false_positive_poc.sh /workspace/argmin returned: poc_exit=0 target_pg_complete_succeeded=0 other_pg_complete_succeeded=1 and FALSE_POSITIVE_CONFIRMED. The helper printed success with pg_id=pg-target even though the target PG had zero complete_succeeded samples. As counter-evidence for introduction, /workspace/validation_artifacts/argmin-uat-backfill-poc/uat_parent_check.sh exercises HEAD^ with min_pg_backfilled=1 and min_pg_completed=1 in the same wrong-PG scenario; it timed out and exited 2. Crash/valgrind/debugger attempts were considered: this is Bash UAT logic, not a memory-safety path; bash -n scripts/uat-s3-tests succeeded, and valgrind/gdb/bashdb are not installed. The PoC includes a non-interactive bash set -x trace as dynamic evidence of the success branch.

